IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rtw-dates`

-- Return to Work Act 2014 (SA), with the Return to Work Regulations 2015 -- SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE.
--
-- The rules are written in the Act's own actors and terms: "the worker", "the employer" (the pre-injury employer in
-- s 18), "the Corporation" (the Return to Work Corporation of South Australia, which trades as ReturnToWorkSA). Where
-- the text says "must" or sets a period, there is a regulative rule (DEONTIC) with the worker, the employer and the
-- Corporation as parties. The Corporation is a party to two rules (ss 31(4) and 32(2); s 48(9)) only so that what the
-- worker is owed can be traced; it has no seat. The injured worker's questions are in rtw-seat.l4 and the employer's in
-- rtw-seat-employer.l4; both IMPORT this module and restate no rule.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED. s 4(1) (worker, employer, contract of service, business day, notional weekly earnings, child and
-- the other terms used), s 4(2), (4), (9), (17); s 5(1), (3), (12)-(16) with regs 7 and 9; s 7(1), (2), (4), (7)-(10);
-- s 16(1)-(4), (6) with reg 11; s 18(1)-(4e) with reg 12; s 20; s 21(2), (3), (5), (8); s 30(1)-(6), (10) with reg 19;
-- s 31(4); s 32(2); s 33(20), (21) with reg 23; s 35 with reg 25; ss 36-39; s 40 with reg 26; s 41; s 42 with reg 27;
-- s 43; s 44; s 48(1)-(10), (12) with reg 28; s 55(2)-(4), (8), (9); s 56(1)-(3), (10)-(12) (the s 56(4) formula is
-- missing, so the lump sum answers `not covered`); ss 57, 58(1)-(4), (6), (7), (11) with reg 34 and Schedule 1 of the
-- regulations; s 59(1), (5)-(7); s 61(1)-(8); s 62 with reg 35; s 72(1), (3); s 100; Schedules 6, 7 and 8 of the Act;
-- regs 4, 5, 6, 8.
--
-- Edition: Return to Work Act 2014 (SA), the Open Australian Legal Corpus text as at 2024-12-01 (version_id
-- south_australian_legislation:2024-12-01/2014.16.un, scraped 2025-03-10), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/return-to-work-act-2014.txt; Return to Work Regulations 2015 (SA), the corpus text as at
-- 2024-12-01 (version_id south_australian_legislation:2024-12-01/2015.29.un, scraped 2025-03-10), as deposited at
-- ../../../return-to-work-regulations-2015/registers/source-bundle/return-to-work-regulations-2015.txt. Neither is the
-- official text, and either may be out of date.
--
-- NUMBERS. Every amount the Act or the regulations mark "(indexed)" is the stated sum adjusted each 1 January by the
-- Adelaide CPI (s 4(17), reg 8; reg 4). The CPI figures are not deposited, so they are INPUTS, and every indexed amount
-- after 2024-12-01 is an input in that sense. Also INPUTS: State average weekly earnings (s 4(9)), the Federal minimum
-- wage (s 4(8), reg 7), the age pension age (Social Security Act 1991 (Cth)), the prime bank rate (reg 3), the overtime
-- component of average weekly earnings (the s 5(12)(b) formula is missing), each degree of whole person impairment
-- (assessed under s 22), and South Australia's public holidays.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: Part 3 service standards in detail, redemptions (ss 53, 54), s 56A elections (except that an election
-- takes a seriously injured worker out of "prescribed seriously injured worker"), Part 5 beyond s 72, Tribunal procedure,
-- Parts 7 onward (registration, premiums including the s 142 formula, self-insurance, the Corporation).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, design defaults of 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage
-- table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Return to Work Act 2014 (SA) -- seat-neutral core`

§§ `s 4(17), regs 4 and 8 -- indexed amounts`

-- s 4(17): a sum "followed by the word "(indexed)" ... is to be adjusted as at 1 January in each year so that the
-- adjusted sum bears to the sum fixed by Parliament the same proportion as the Consumer Price Index for the September
-- quarter of the immediately preceding year bears to the Consumer Price Index for the September quarter of the year
-- immediately preceding the year in which the law fixing the sum took effect, with the amount so adjusted being rounded
-- up under a scheme prescribed by the regulations". Reg 8: "rounded up to the nearest dollar".
-- Reg 4 (sums in the regulations): "adjusted on 1 January of each year, beginning on 1 January 2016, by multiplying the
-- stated amount by a proportion obtained by dividing the Consumer Price Index for the September quarter of the
-- immediately preceding year by the Consumer Price Index for the September quarter of 2014 (with the amount so adjusted
-- being rounded up to the nearest dollar)". s 4(1): the CPI is "the Consumer Price Index (All groups index for Adelaide)".
-- The two index figures are INPUTS. For a day before the first adjustment, give the same figure twice.
DECLARE `CPI figures` HAS
    `the CPI for the September quarter before the adjustment` IS A NUMBER
    `the CPI for the base September quarter`                 IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the stated sum` IS A NUMBER, `the CPI` IS A `CPI figures`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the stated sum` `indexed by` `the CPI` MEANS
    CEILING (`the stated sum` TIMES `the CPI`'s `the CPI for the September quarter before the adjustment` DIVIDED BY `the CPI`'s `the CPI for the base September quarter`)

-- Rounding half up, used where the Act or the regulations round to a stated place and do not say which way.
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, `places` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded half up` x `to` `places` `decimal places` MEANS
    FLOOR ((x TIMES (`ten to the power` `places`)) PLUS 0.5) DIVIDED BY (`ten to the power` `places`)

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`ten to the power` n MEANS `power` 10 n

-- A whole-number power, by repeated multiplication, so that the result stays exact.
GIVEN b IS A NUMBER, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`power` b n MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN 1
    ELSE b TIMES (`power` b (n MINUS 1))

-- The n-th entry of a table row (1-based); 0 past the end (never reached: callers check the range).
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the row` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`entry` `n` `of` `the row` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the row`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY xs THEN
        IF `n` AT MOST 1
        THEN x
        ELSE `entry` (`n` MINUS 1) `of` xs

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a whole number` x IF FLOOR x EQUALS x

§§ `s 4(1), (2), (4) and regs 5, 6 -- worker and employer`

-- s 4(1): "worker means-- (a) a person by whom work is done under a contract of service (whether or not as an
-- employee); (b) a person who is a worker by virtue of Schedule 1; (c) a self-employed worker". "contract of service
-- means-- (a) a contract under which 1 person (the worker) is employed by another (the employer); or (b) a contract,
-- arrangement or understanding under which 1 person (the worker) works for another in prescribed work or work of a
-- prescribed class; or (c) a contract of apprenticeship; or (d) a contract, arrangement or understanding under which a
-- person (the worker)-- (i) receives on-the-job training in a trade or vocation from another (the employer); and (ii) is
-- during the period of that training remunerated by the employer". "apprentice includes ... a trainee". "self-employed
-- worker means a person to whom the Corporation has extended the protection of this Act pursuant to section 175".
-- s 4(2): "A member of the crew of a fishing boat who is remunerated by a share in profits or gross receipts obtained by
-- working the boat is not a worker for the purposes of this Act."
--
-- Reg 5(1): the prescribed classes of work for paragraph (b), each (other than (g)) where "(i) the work is performed by 1
-- person ... (the worker) in the course of or for the purposes of a trade or business carried on by another person ...
-- (the employer); and (ii) the work is performed personally by the worker ...; and (iii) the worker does not employ any
-- other person to carry out any part of the work", with a cap on the materials the worker supplies:
--   (a) building work, other than wall or floor tiling: materials not more than 4% of the total payable or $120
--       (indexed), "whichever is the greater", and no single tool or item of plant over $18 988 (indexed);
--   (b) cleaning work: materials not more than $120 (indexed), or $60 (indexed) for window cleaning, for a term of not
--       more than 1 month, or "an average of" that amount per month for a longer term;
--   (c) driving a goods vehicle where the driver is paid under the Local Government Employees Award or the Adelaide City
--       Corporation Award; (d) driving a taxi-cab where the driver "does not hold or lease a licence"; (f) performing as
--       an entertainer at a hotel, restaurant, club or similar venue: materials not more than $120 (indexed);
--   (e) driving or riding a vehicle, other than a commercial motor vehicle, to carry goods, where the driver "does not
--       simultaneously own or operate more than 1 vehicle for work purposes": materials not more than $120 (indexed),
--       and the goods "are not owned (and have not been previously owned)" by the driver or the employer;
--   (g) "thoroughbred riding work where the work is performed by a licensed jockey" (TRSA is the presumptive employer,
--       reg 5(3)).
-- Reg 5(4): outwork governed by an award or industrial agreement for outworkers "is prescribed work". Reg 5(5): "Subject to
-- regulation 6, the work of a minister, priest or other member of a religious order is a prescribed class of work".
-- The $120, $60 and $18 988 are indexed under reg 4.
DECLARE `Prescribed class of work` IS ONE OF
    `none of the regulation 5 classes`
    `building work other than wall or floor tiling`
    `window cleaning work`
    `cleaning work other than window cleaning`
    `driving a goods vehicle while paid under a local government award`
    `driving a taxi or similar vehicle without holding or leasing its licence`
    `driving or riding a vehicle other than a commercial motor vehicle to carry goods`
    `performing as an entertainer at a hotel, restaurant, club or similar venue`
    `thoroughbred riding work by a licensed jockey`
    `outwork governed by an award or industrial agreement for outworkers`
    `the work of a minister, priest or other member of a religious order`

-- Reg 6: "the following persons are excluded from the application of the Act": (1) a minister of the Anglican Church, a
-- priest or member of a religious order of the Catholic Church, a pastor of the Lutheran Church, an ordained minister,
-- deaconess or lay pastor of the Uniting Church in an approved placement, each in South Australia; (2) "a worker who is
-- employed by an employer to participate as a contestant in a sporting or athletic activity", except (3) a rider or
-- driver authorised by a racing controlling authority, or "a boxer or wrestler employed or engaged for a fee"; (4) a
-- driver carrying goods for a principal's trade or business in a commercial motor vehicle that the driver owns, leases or
-- hires, if the vehicle is not supplied (directly or indirectly) by the principal or a person related to it and the goods
-- "are not owned (and have not been previously owned) by the driver or by the principal"; (6) a person to whom the
-- Seafarers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1992 (Cth) applies.
DECLARE `Regulation 6 class` IS ONE OF
    `none of the regulation 6 classes`
    `a minister, priest, pastor or deaconess named in regulation 6(1)`
    `a contestant employed for a sporting or athletic activity`
    `a contestant who is a licensed race rider or driver, or a boxer or wrestler engaged for a fee`
    `a driver carrying goods in a commercial motor vehicle the driver owns, leases or hires`
    `a person to whom the Seafarers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1992 applies`

DECLARE `Engagement facts` HAS
    `employed by the other person`                                             IS A BOOLEAN -- contract of service (a)
    `an apprentice or trainee under a contract of apprenticeship`              IS A BOOLEAN -- (c)
    `paid while receiving on-the-job training in a trade or vocation from the other person` IS A BOOLEAN -- (d)
    `the class of work`                                                        IS A `Prescribed class of work` -- (b), reg 5
    `the work is done for the purposes of the other person's trade or business` IS A BOOLEAN -- reg 5(1)(i)
    `the work is done personally`                                              IS A BOOLEAN -- reg 5(1)(ii)
    `someone else is employed to do part of the work`                          IS A BOOLEAN -- reg 5(1)(iii)
    `the value of the materials supplied`                                      IS A NUMBER  -- reg 5(1)(iv)
    `the total payable under the arrangement`                                  IS A NUMBER  -- reg 5(1)(a)(iv)(A)
    `the value of the most valuable tool or item of plant or equipment`        IS A NUMBER  -- reg 5(1)(a)(v)
    `the term of the arrangement in months`                                    IS A NUMBER  -- reg 5(1)(b)(iv)
    `more than 1 vehicle is owned or operated for work at the same time`       IS A BOOLEAN -- reg 5(1)(e)
    `the goods are or were owned by the driver or by the other person`         IS A BOOLEAN -- reg 5(1)(e)(v), 6(4)(d)
    `the vehicle is supplied by the other person or someone related to it`     IS A BOOLEAN -- reg 6(4)(c)
    `a fishing crew member paid by a share of profits or gross receipts`       IS A BOOLEAN -- s 4(2)
    `a volunteer of whom the Crown is the presumptive employer under Schedule 1` IS A BOOLEAN -- worker (b)
    `the Corporation has extended the Act's protection to the person under s 175` IS A BOOLEAN -- worker (c)
    `the regulation 6 class`                                                   IS A `Regulation 6 class`

GIVEN f IS AN `Engagement facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conditions common to regulation 5(1)(a) to (f) are met` f IF
        f's `the work is done for the purposes of the other person's trade or business`
    AND f's `the work is done personally`
    AND (NOT f's `someone else is employed to do part of the work`)

-- Reg 5(1)(b)(iv): for a term of not more than 1 month, the materials; for a longer term, their average per month.
GIVEN `the monthly cap` IS A NUMBER, f IS AN `Engagement facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the materials are within the cleaning cap of` `the monthly cap` `for` f IF
    IF f's `the term of the arrangement in months` AT MOST 1
    THEN f's `the value of the materials supplied` AT MOST `the monthly cap`
    ELSE (f's `the value of the materials supplied` DIVIDED BY f's `the term of the arrangement in months`) AT MOST `the monthly cap`

GIVEN f IS AN `Engagement facts`, `the CPI` IS A `CPI figures`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the work is in a regulation 5 prescribed class` f `the CPI` IF
    CONSIDER f's `the class of work`
    WHEN `none of the regulation 5 classes` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `building work other than wall or floor tiling` THEN
            `the conditions common to regulation 5(1)(a) to (f) are met` f
        AND f's `the value of the materials supplied` AT MOST (max (f's `the total payable under the arrangement` TIMES 4%) (120 `indexed by` `the CPI`))
        AND f's `the value of the most valuable tool or item of plant or equipment` AT MOST (18988 `indexed by` `the CPI`)
    WHEN `window cleaning work` THEN
            `the conditions common to regulation 5(1)(a) to (f) are met` f
        AND `the materials are within the cleaning cap of` (60 `indexed by` `the CPI`) `for` f
    WHEN `cleaning work other than window cleaning` THEN
            `the conditions common to regulation 5(1)(a) to (f) are met` f
        AND `the materials are within the cleaning cap of` (120 `indexed by` `the CPI`) `for` f
    WHEN `driving or riding a vehicle other than a commercial motor vehicle to carry goods` THEN
            `the conditions common to regulation 5(1)(a) to (f) are met` f
        AND f's `the value of the materials supplied` AT MOST (120 `indexed by` `the CPI`)
        AND (NOT f's `more than 1 vehicle is owned or operated for work at the same time`)
        AND (NOT f's `the goods are or were owned by the driver or by the other person`)
    WHEN `thoroughbred riding work by a licensed jockey` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `outwork governed by an award or industrial agreement for outworkers` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the work of a minister, priest or other member of a religious order` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE
            `the conditions common to regulation 5(1)(a) to (f) are met` f
        AND f's `the value of the materials supplied` AT MOST (120 `indexed by` `the CPI`)

GIVEN f IS AN `Engagement facts`, `the CPI` IS A `CPI figures`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the work is done under a contract of service` f `the CPI` IF
        f's `employed by the other person`
    OR  `the work is in a regulation 5 prescribed class` f `the CPI`
    OR  f's `an apprentice or trainee under a contract of apprenticeship`
    OR  f's `paid while receiving on-the-job training in a trade or vocation from the other person`

GIVEN f IS AN `Engagement facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is excluded by regulation 6` f IF
    CONSIDER f's `the regulation 6 class`
    WHEN `none of the regulation 6 classes` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a contestant who is a licensed race rider or driver, or a boxer or wrestler engaged for a fee` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a driver carrying goods in a commercial motor vehicle the driver owns, leases or hires` THEN
            (NOT f's `the vehicle is supplied by the other person or someone related to it`)
        AND (NOT f's `the goods are or were owned by the driver or by the other person`)
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN f IS AN `Engagement facts`, `the CPI` IS A `CPI figures`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a worker` f `the CPI` IF
        (    `the work is done under a contract of service` f `the CPI`
         OR  f's `a volunteer of whom the Crown is the presumptive employer under Schedule 1`
         OR  f's `the Corporation has extended the Act's protection to the person under s 175`)
    AND (NOT f's `a fishing crew member paid by a share of profits or gross receipts`)
    AND (NOT `the person is excluded by regulation 6` f)

-- s 4(4): "Where in a prescribed industry or in prescribed circumstances a person (the principal) contracts with another
-- person (the contractor) for the performance by the contractor of work undertaken by the principal, the principal will,
-- for the purposes of this Act, be taken to be the employer of workers employed by the contractor." Reg 5(8): "a
-- prescribed circumstance is where a person (the principal) contracts with another person (the contractor) who is not
-- registered as an employer under the Act." No industry is prescribed in the deposited regulations.
GIVEN `the principal contracted the contractor to do work the principal undertook` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contractor is registered as an employer under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the principal is taken to be the employer of the contractor's workers` `the principal contracted the contractor to do work the principal undertook` `the contractor is registered as an employer under the Act` IF
    `the principal contracted the contractor to do work the principal undertook` AND (NOT `the contractor is registered as an employer under the Act`)

§§ `s 5 and regs 7, 9 -- average weekly earnings`

-- s 5(1): "the average weekly earnings of an injured worker is the average weekly amount that the worker earned during the
-- period of 12 months preceding the relevant date in relevant employment" (all the worker's employers at the time, s 5(2));
-- s 5(3): leave pay is earnings; s 5(4)-(11) change the period or the rate in particular cases (the caller gives the
-- earnings and weeks of the period that applies). s 5(12)(a): overtime is disregarded if the worker "had no reasonable
-- expectation to work overtime within the foreseeable future", otherwise taken into account; (b): "the component for
-- overtime will be an amount calculated as follows:" -- the formula is MISSING from the deposit (see
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/return-to-work-act-2014.formulas.md), so the component is an INPUT. s 5(13): salary
-- sacrificed for superannuation counts; a non-cash benefit of a class in reg 9 counts if the worker does not retain it.
-- s 5(14): employer superannuation contributions and prescribed allowances are disregarded. s 5(15): "(a) ... not less
-- than the weekly wage to which the worker was then entitled under the award or industrial agreement; (b) if ... less than
-- the Federal minimum wage applying in relation to the worker (adjusted ... part-time ... pro-rata ...), ... fixed at the
-- Federal minimum wage" (not for a self-employed worker); "(c) ... in no case ... more than twice State average weekly
-- earnings". Reg 7(2): the part-time adjustment is the hours worked "as a percentage of the number of hours per week
-- that constitute full-time employment ... (calculated to 1 decimal point)" times the Federal minimum wage.
DECLARE `Earnings facts` HAS
    `the earnings in the relevant period, other than overtime`         IS A NUMBER
    `the weeks in the relevant period`                                 IS A NUMBER
    `the weekly value of prescribed non-cash benefits not retained`     IS A NUMBER
    `a reasonable expectation of working overtime`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the overtime component`                                           IS A NUMBER
    `the pay was covered by an award or industrial agreement`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the weekly wage under the award or industrial agreement`          IS A NUMBER
    `a self-employed worker`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the hours worked per week`                                        IS A NUMBER
    `the hours per week that constitute full-time employment`          IS A NUMBER
    `the Federal minimum wage per week`                                IS A NUMBER
    `State average weekly earnings`                                    IS A NUMBER

-- Reg 7(2): READING: "calculated to 1 decimal point" is rounded half up.
GIVEN `the weekly hours` IS A NUMBER, `the full-time hours` IS A NUMBER, `the Federal minimum wage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Federal minimum wage for` `the weekly hours` `hours of` `the full-time hours` `from` `the Federal minimum wage` MEANS
    IF `the weekly hours` LESS THAN `the full-time hours`
    THEN `the Federal minimum wage` TIMES (`rounded half up` (`the weekly hours` DIVIDED BY `the full-time hours` TIMES 100) `to` 1 `decimal places`) DIVIDED BY 100
    ELSE `the Federal minimum wage`

GIVEN e IS AN `Earnings facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the average of the earnings` e MEANS
    (IF e's `the weeks in the relevant period` GREATER THAN 0
     THEN e's `the earnings in the relevant period, other than overtime` DIVIDED BY e's `the weeks in the relevant period`
     ELSE 0)
    PLUS e's `the weekly value of prescribed non-cash benefits not retained`
    PLUS (IF e's `a reasonable expectation of working overtime` THEN e's `the overtime component` ELSE 0)

GIVEN e IS AN `Earnings facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the average weekly earnings under s 5` e MEANS
    min (`after the floors`) (2 TIMES e's `State average weekly earnings`)
    WHERE
        `after the award floor` MEANS
            IF e's `the pay was covered by an award or industrial agreement`
            THEN max (`the average of the earnings` e) (e's `the weekly wage under the award or industrial agreement`)
            ELSE `the average of the earnings` e
        `after the floors` MEANS
            IF e's `a self-employed worker`
            THEN `after the award floor`
            ELSE max `after the award floor` (`the Federal minimum wage for` (e's `the hours worked per week`) `hours of` (e's `the hours per week that constitute full-time employment`) `from` (e's `the Federal minimum wage per week`))

§§ `s 7 -- an injury arising from employment`

-- s 7(1): "This Act applies to an injury if (and only if) it arises from employment." (2): "an injury arises from
-- employment if-- (a) in the case of a physical injury--the injury arises out of or in the course of employment and the
-- employment was a significant contributing cause of the injury; and (b) in the case of a psychiatric injury-- (i) ...
-- arises out of or in the course of employment and the employment was the significant contributing cause of the injury;
-- and (ii) the injury did not arise wholly or predominantly from any action or decision designated under subsection (4)"
-- (reasonable action to transfer, demote, discipline, counsel, retrench or dismiss; reasonable decisions on promotion or
-- benefits; reasonable administrative action; reasonable action under the Act). s 4(1): "psychiatric injury means pure
-- mental harm"; "physical injury means an injury other than a psychiatric injury".
-- (7): no injury arises from employment "out of or in the course of the worker's involvement in a social or sporting
-- activity, except where the activity forms part of the worker's employment or is undertaken at the direction or request
-- of the employer". (8): an injury on a journey "arises from employment if (and only if)-- (a) the journey is undertaken
-- in the course of carrying out duties of employment; or (b) the journey is between [the residence or place of
-- employment and the places listed] ..., and there is a real and substantial connection between the employment and the
-- journey". (10): a (b) journey "must be ... by a reasonably direct route" with no substantial deviation that materially
-- increases the risk. READING (finding 4): the "real and substantial connection" words stand at the margin after (b), so
-- they are read as qualifying both (a) and (b); and for a journey, s 7(8) is the whole test ("if (and only if)").
DECLARE `Kind of injury` IS ONE OF `a physical injury`, `a psychiatric injury`

DECLARE `Injury facts` HAS
    `the kind of injury`                                                     IS A `Kind of injury`
    `it arose out of or in the course of employment`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `employment was a significant contributing cause`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `employment was the significant contributing cause`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `it arose wholly or predominantly from reasonable action or decisions of the kinds in s 7(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it arose from a social or sporting activity`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the activity was part of the employment or at the employer's direction or request` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it arose on a journey`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the journey was in the course of carrying out duties of employment`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the journey was between places listed in s 7(8)(b)`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the route was reasonably direct without a substantial, riskier deviation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is a real and substantial connection between the employment and the journey` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN i IS AN `Injury facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the injury arises from employment` i IF
    IF i's `it arose on a journey`
    THEN    (    i's `the journey was in the course of carrying out duties of employment`
             OR  (i's `the journey was between places listed in s 7(8)(b)` AND i's `the route was reasonably direct without a substantial, riskier deviation`))
        AND i's `there is a real and substantial connection between the employment and the journey`
    ELSE IF i's `it arose from a social or sporting activity` AND (NOT i's `the activity was part of the employment or at the employer's direction or request`)
         THEN FALSE
         ELSE CONSIDER i's `the kind of injury`
              WHEN `a physical injury` THEN
                  i's `it arose out of or in the course of employment` AND i's `employment was a significant contributing cause`
              WHEN `a psychiatric injury` THEN
                      i's `it arose out of or in the course of employment`
                  AND i's `employment was the significant contributing cause`
                  AND (NOT i's `it arose wholly or predominantly from reasonable action or decisions of the kinds in s 7(4)`)

§§ `s 16 and reg 11 -- notice of the injury`

-- s 16(1): "If a worker suffers a work injury, notice of that injury must be given-- (a) to the employer by whom the
-- worker is employed at the time of the occurrence of the injury; or (b) if the worker is not in employment or is
-- self-employed--to the Corporation." (2): "Notice of an injury should be given-- (a) if practicable within 24 hours
-- after the occurrence of the injury but, if that is not practicable, as soon as practicable after the occurrence of the
-- injury; (b) if the worker is not, immediately after the occurrence of the injury, aware of the injury--as soon as
-- practicable after the worker becomes so aware". What is "practicable" is a judgment: an INPUT, in hours.
DECLARE `Notice recipient` IS ONE OF
    `the employer by whom the worker was employed when the injury occurred`
    `the Corporation`

GIVEN `in employment at the time of the injury` IS A BOOLEAN, `self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Notice recipient`
`to whom notice of the injury must be given` `in employment at the time of the injury` `self-employed` MEANS
    IF `in employment at the time of the injury` AND (NOT `self-employed`)
    THEN `the employer by whom the worker was employed when the injury occurred`
    ELSE `the Corporation`

-- The hours, from the injury (or from when the worker became aware of it, s 16(2)(b)), within which notice should be given.
GIVEN `notice within 24 hours was practicable` IS A BOOLEAN, `the hours within which notice was practicable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the hours within which notice should be given` `notice within 24 hours was practicable` `the hours within which notice was practicable` MEANS
    IF `notice within 24 hours was practicable` THEN 24 ELSE `the hours within which notice was practicable`

-- s 16(4): notice "will be taken to have been given to an employer if-- (a) it is given to-- (i) the employer at any place
-- of business of the employer; or (ii) any person under whose supervision the worker was employed at the time of the
-- injury; or (iii) any person designated for the purpose by the worker's employer; or (b) it is given to the employer in
-- the manner prescribed by the regulations." Reg 11: "if it is served-- (a) by post on the employer; or (b) by email sent
-- to an address used by the employer in the ordinary course of business."
DECLARE `Manner of giving notice` IS ONE OF
    `to the employer at a place of business of the employer`
    `to the person who supervised the worker when the injury occurred`
    `to a person the employer designated for the purpose`
    `by post on the employer`
    `by email to an address the employer uses in the ordinary course of business`
    `in some other way`

GIVEN m IS A `Manner of giving notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `notice given this way is taken to have been given to the employer` m IF
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN `in some other way` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 16(6): "if an employer (not being a self-insured employer) receives notice of an injury ... the employer must, within
-- 5 business days after the receipt of the notice, send a copy of the notice to the Corporation. Maximum penalty: $1 500."
-- s 30(5) and (6) carry the same maximum penalty.
`the maximum penalty under ss 16(6), 30(5) and 30(6)` MEANS 1500

§§ `s 21 -- a seriously injured worker`

-- s 21(2): "a seriously injured worker is a worker-- (a) in the case of psychiatric injury--whose work injury or injuries
-- have resulted in permanent impairment and the degree of whole person impairment has been assessed under Division 5 ...
-- to be 30% or more; or (b) in the case of physical injury-- ... 35% or more." (8): physical and psychiatric impairment
-- are assessed separately, without consequential mental harm. (3): pending an assessment, the Corporation may make "an
-- interim decision to the effect that the worker will be taken to be a seriously injured worker"; (5): otherwise "the
-- worker will be taken not to be a seriously injured worker". The degree of impairment is assessed by an accredited
-- medical practitioner under s 22: an INPUT.
-- The 35% for physical injury came with the Return to Work (Scheme Sustainability) Amendment Act 2022 (No 4 of 2022),
-- Schedule 1 clause 2: the amendments to s 21(2), (8), s 72 and Schedule 7 "apply in relation to any work injury where
-- the final examination ... occurs on or after the designated day" (a day appointed by proclamation; it is not in the
-- deposit). For an earlier final examination of a physical injury (a physical impairment above 0%), the threshold that
-- applied is not in the deposited text: `not covered` (finding 10). Clause 2 does not apply to psychiatric injuries
-- (clause 2(1)).
DECLARE `Impairment facts` HAS
    `the whole person impairment from physical injury, in per cent`     IS A NUMBER
    `the whole person impairment from psychiatric injury, in per cent`  IS A NUMBER
    `the final examination was on or after the 2022 designated day`     IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Seriously injured answer` IS ONE OF
    `a seriously injured worker (s 21(2))`
    `taken to be a seriously injured worker by an interim decision (s 21(3))`
    `not a seriously injured worker (s 21(5))`
    `not covered: the threshold for a physical injury whose final examination was before the 2022 designated day is not in the deposited text`

GIVEN p IS AN `Impairment facts`, `an interim decision is in effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Seriously injured answer`
`the s 21 answer for` p `with an interim decision` `an interim decision is in effect` MEANS
    IF p's `the whole person impairment from psychiatric injury, in per cent` AT LEAST 30
    THEN `a seriously injured worker (s 21(2))`
    ELSE IF `an interim decision is in effect`
         THEN `taken to be a seriously injured worker by an interim decision (s 21(3))`
         ELSE IF (NOT p's `the final examination was on or after the 2022 designated day`) AND p's `the whole person impairment from physical injury, in per cent` GREATER THAN 0
              THEN `not covered: the threshold for a physical injury whose final examination was before the 2022 designated day is not in the deposited text`
              ELSE IF p's `the whole person impairment from physical injury, in per cent` AT LEAST 35
                   THEN `a seriously injured worker (s 21(2))`
                   ELSE `not a seriously injured worker (s 21(5))`

GIVEN a IS A `Seriously injured answer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the answer makes a seriously injured worker` a IF
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `a seriously injured worker (s 21(2))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `taken to be a seriously injured worker by an interim decision (s 21(3))` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 30 and reg 19 -- the claim`

-- s 30(1): a claim "(a) must be made in a manner and form approved by the Corporation; and (b) must be made within the
-- prescribed period; and (c) must be supported by a certificate in the designated form by a designated person". (10):
-- "prescribed period ... means the period of 6 months commencing on the day on which the entitlement to make the claim
-- arises". When the entitlement arises is an INPUT. READING: the period's last day (rtw-dates.l4).
GIVEN `the entitlement day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to make the claim` `the entitlement day` MEANS
    `the last day of the period of` 6 `months commencing on` `the entitlement day`

GIVEN `the entitlement day` IS A DATE, `the claim day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim was made within the prescribed period` `the entitlement day` `the claim day` IF
        (`the entitlement day` `is on or before` `the claim day`)
    AND (`the claim day` `is on or before` (`the last day to make the claim` `the entitlement day`))

-- s 30(2): "If a notice of an injury is required under this Act, a claim may not be made in respect of that injury unless
-- notice of the injury has been given as required." (3): "Despite subsections (1) and (2)-- (a) the absence of, or a defect
-- in, a notice of injury is not a bar to the making of a claim if-- (i) the proper determination of the claim has not been
-- substantially prejudiced; or (ii) the failure to give the notice, or the defect in the notice, was occasioned by
-- ignorance of the claimant, mistake or absence from the State, or other reasonable cause; and (b) a failure to make a
-- claim within the prescribed period is not a bar to the making of a claim if [the same two grounds]". Whether the
-- determination was prejudiced, or the cause reasonable, is decided by others: INPUTS.
DECLARE `Claim facts` HAS
    `the day the entitlement to make the claim arose`                           IS A DATE
    `the day the claim was given`                                              IS A DATE
    `notice of the injury was given`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proper determination of the claim has not been substantially prejudiced` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the failure to give notice came from ignorance, mistake, absence from the State or other reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lateness came from ignorance, mistake, absence from the State or other reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Claim answer` IS ONE OF
    `the claim may be made`
    `the claim may be made: s 30(3) excuses the lateness or the want of notice`
    `barred: the claim is late and s 30(3)(b) does not excuse it`
    `barred: notice of the injury was not given and s 30(3)(a) does not excuse it`

GIVEN c IS A `Claim facts`
GIVETH A `Claim answer`
`the s 30 answer for` c MEANS
    IF (NOT `on time`) AND (NOT `lateness excused`)
    THEN `barred: the claim is late and s 30(3)(b) does not excuse it`
    ELSE IF (NOT c's `notice of the injury was given`) AND (NOT `want of notice excused`)
         THEN `barred: notice of the injury was not given and s 30(3)(a) does not excuse it`
         ELSE IF `on time` AND c's `notice of the injury was given`
              THEN `the claim may be made`
              ELSE `the claim may be made: s 30(3) excuses the lateness or the want of notice`
    WHERE
        `on time` MEANS `the claim was made within the prescribed period` (c's `the day the entitlement to make the claim arose`) (c's `the day the claim was given`)
        `lateness excused` MEANS
                c's `the proper determination of the claim has not been substantially prejudiced`
            OR  c's `the lateness came from ignorance, mistake, absence from the State or other reasonable cause`
        `want of notice excused` MEANS
                c's `the proper determination of the claim has not been substantially prejudiced`
            OR  c's `the failure to give notice came from ignorance, mistake, absence from the State or other reasonable cause`

-- s 30(4): "A claim must be given at first instance as follows: (a) where the worker is at the commencement of the
-- incapacity in employment--the claim must be given to the employer; (b) in any other case--the claim must be given to the
-- Corporation."
DECLARE `Claim recipient` IS ONE OF `the employer`, `the Corporation, not the employer`

GIVEN `in employment when the incapacity commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Claim recipient`
`to whom the claim must be given` `in employment when the incapacity commenced` MEANS
    IF `in employment when the incapacity commenced` THEN `the employer` ELSE `the Corporation, not the employer`

-- s 30(1)(c), (10): the certificate is by "a designated person", meaning "(a) a recognised health practitioner; or (b)
-- another person of a prescribed class acting in prescribed circumstances". Reg 19: a nurse practitioner is of a
-- prescribed class and may certify "if the nurse practitioner has examined the worker at-- (i) an incorporated hospital;
-- or (ii) a private hospital", but only "certifying the worker's capacity for work over the ensuing 7 days".
DECLARE `Certifier` IS ONE OF
    `a recognised health practitioner`
    `a nurse practitioner who examined the worker at an incorporated or private hospital`
    `someone else`

DECLARE `Certificate answer` IS ONE OF
    `a designated person may certify the claim`
    `a designated person may certify the claim, but the capacity certified covers only the next 7 days`
    `not a designated person`

GIVEN c IS A `Certifier`
GIVETH A `Certificate answer`
`who may certify the claim` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `a recognised health practitioner` THEN `a designated person may certify the claim`
    WHEN `a nurse practitioner who examined the worker at an incorporated or private hospital` THEN `a designated person may certify the claim, but the capacity certified covers only the next 7 days`
    WHEN `someone else` THEN `not a designated person`

-- s 30(5): "Within 5 business days after receipt of a claim under this section, an employer (not being a self-insured
-- employer) must forward to the Corporation-- (a) a copy of the claim; (b) a statement in the designated form. Maximum
-- penalty: $1 500." s 16(6) has the same 5 business days for a copy of the notice of injury.
DECLARE `Forwarding answer` IS ONE OF
    `the employer must forward it to the Corporation no later than` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `no duty to forward: the employer is a self-insured employer`
    `no duty to forward: the claim is given to the Corporation, not the employer`

GIVEN `the day the employer received it` IS A DATE, `weekday public holidays in the 5 business days` IS A NUMBER, `is self-insured` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Forwarding answer`
`the employer's 5 business days after receiving it on` `the day the employer received it` `with public holidays` `weekday public holidays in the 5 business days` `self-insured` `is self-insured` MEANS
    IF `is self-insured`
    THEN `no duty to forward: the employer is a self-insured employer`
    ELSE `the employer must forward it to the Corporation no later than` (`the last of` 5 `business days after` `the day the employer received it` `with public holidays` `weekday public holidays in the 5 business days`)

§§ `ss 31(4), 32(2) -- determining an income support claim, and interim payments`

-- s 31(4): "The Corporation must determine claims for compensation as expeditiously as reasonably practicable and where
-- the claim is for compensation by way of income support must, wherever practicable, endeavour to determine the claim
-- within 10 business days after the date of receipt of the claim." s 32(2): "The Corporation must offer to make interim
-- payments under this section if it fails to determine the relevant claim within 10 business days after the date of
-- receipt of the claim." No seat for the Corporation: this is the day that matters to the worker.
GIVEN `the day the Corporation received the claim` IS A DATE, `weekday public holidays in the 10 business days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the 10th business day after the Corporation received the claim on` `the day the Corporation received the claim` `with public holidays` `weekday public holidays in the 10 business days` MEANS
    `the last of` 10 `business days after` `the day the Corporation received the claim` `with public holidays` `weekday public holidays in the 10 business days`

§§ `s 33(20), (21) and reg 23 -- how long medical expenses are paid`

-- s 33(20): "an entitlement to compensation under this section ... comes to an end if the worker has not had an
-- entitlement to receive weekly payments in relation to the work injury under Division 4 for a continuous period of 12
-- months (or has not had an entitlement to receive weekly payments under Division 4 and a period of 12 months has
-- expired) (insofar as costs are incurred after the end of that period)." READING: the 12 months run from the day after
-- the last day of an entitlement to weekly payments, or, for a worker who never had one, from the day of the injury.
-- (21): (20) "(a) does not apply in relation to a seriously injured worker; and (b) does not apply-- (i) in relation to any
-- therapeutic appliance required to maintain the worker's capacity; or (ii) in relation to surgery, [and associated
-- services], where the Corporation has determined or accepted, on application made before the end of the period ..., that
-- it is reasonable and appropriate for such surgery to be undertaken at a later time ...; or (iii) in relation to
-- prescribed classes of injury, where the Corporation has determined or accepted, on application made before the end of
-- the period ..., that it is reasonable and appropriate for the services to be provided after the end of that period ...;
-- or (iv) in any other circumstances prescribed by the regulations." Reg 23(1) prescribes, for (iii): multiple myeloma,
-- primary leukaemia, primary non-Hodgkin's lymphoma, primary site bladder, brain, breast, colorectal, kidney, oesophageal,
-- prostate, testicular and ureter cancer, and pneumoconiosis (including silicosis) and other injuries caused by exposure
-- to crystalline silica. Reg 23(2b), for (iv): "travel and accommodation costs incurred by a worker in attending an
-- assessment for permanent impairment". Reg 23(2), (2a) (injuries before 1 July 2015) are not encoded.
DECLARE `Kind of medical cost` IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary medical cost`
    `a therapeutic appliance required to maintain the worker's capacity`
    `later surgery the Corporation accepted on an application made before the period ended`
    `services the Corporation accepted, on an application made before the period ended, for an injury of a class in regulation 23(1)`
    `travel and accommodation to attend a permanent impairment assessment`

DECLARE `Medical period facts` HAS
    `a seriously injured worker`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day of the injury`                                       IS A DATE
    `there was an entitlement to weekly payments`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the last day of the entitlement to weekly payments`          IS A DATE
    `the kind of cost`                                            IS A `Kind of medical cost`
    `the day the cost is incurred`                                IS A DATE

GIVEN m IS A `Medical period facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the s 33(20) period for` m MEANS
    `the last day of the period of` 12 `months commencing on` `the start`
    WHERE
        `the start` MEANS
            IF m's `there was an entitlement to weekly payments`
            THEN (m's `the last day of the entitlement to weekly payments`) `plus days` 1
            ELSE m's `the day of the injury`

GIVEN m IS A `Medical period facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the cost is within the period for medical expenses` m IF
        m's `a seriously injured worker`
    OR  `excepted`
    OR  ((m's `the day the cost is incurred`) `is on or before` (`the last day of the s 33(20) period for` m))
    WHERE
        `excepted` MEANS
            CONSIDER m's `the kind of cost`
            WHEN `an ordinary medical cost` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `s 35 and reg 25 -- property damage`

-- s 35(1): if, "in consequence of the trauma out of which the injury arose, damage occurs to any therapeutic appliances,
-- clothes, personal effects or tools of trade of the worker, the worker is, subject to limitations prescribed by
-- regulation, entitled to be compensated for the full amount of the damage." (2): not "damage to a motor vehicle".
-- Reg 25: "(a) for damage to therapeutic appliances and tools of trade--no limit; (b) for damage to clothes and personal
-- effects--$2 374 (indexed) in total."
GIVEN `the damage to therapeutic appliances and tools of trade` IS A NUMBER, `the damage to clothes and personal effects` IS A NUMBER, `the CPI` IS A `CPI figures`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the property damage compensation for` `the damage to therapeutic appliances and tools of trade` `and` `the damage to clothes and personal effects` `with` `the CPI` MEANS
    `the damage to therapeutic appliances and tools of trade` PLUS (min `the damage to clothes and personal effects` (2374 `indexed by` `the CPI`))

§§ `ss 36-39, 41, 42 and reg 27 -- weekly payments`

-- s 36: "(1) ... the current work capacity of a worker is constituted by a present inability arising from a work injury
-- such that the worker is not able to return to his or her employment at the time of the occurrence of the injury but is
-- able to return to work in suitable employment. (2) ... a worker has no current work capacity if the worker has a present
-- inability arising from a work injury such that the worker is not able to return to work, either in his or her
-- employment at the time of the occurrence of the injury or in suitable employment."
DECLARE `Work capacity` IS ONE OF
    `not incapacitated for work`
    `a current work capacity`
    `no current work capacity`

GIVEN `able to return to the pre-injury employment` IS A BOOLEAN, `able to work in suitable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Work capacity`
`the work capacity of a worker` `able to return to the pre-injury employment` `able to work in suitable employment` MEANS
    IF `able to return to the pre-injury employment`
    THEN `not incapacitated for work`
    ELSE IF `able to work in suitable employment`
         THEN `a current work capacity`
         ELSE `no current work capacity`

-- s 39(1) (a worker other than a seriously injured worker): in the first designated period of 52 weeks from the date
-- incapacity first occurs, "(i) ... no current work capacity--... weekly payments equal to the worker's notional weekly
-- earnings; and (ii) ... a current work capacity--... the difference between the worker's notional weekly earnings and the
-- worker's designated weekly earnings"; in the second designated period, the next 52 weeks, 80% of each. (3): "no
-- entitlement ... after the end of the period of 104 weeks". s 41(1) (a seriously injured worker): the same in the first
-- 52 weeks, then 80% "for any period", without end. s 39(2), 41(2): designated weekly earnings are "the current weekly
-- earnings of the worker in employment or self-employment (if any) but not so as to include a prescribed benefit" (s 37:
-- leave, retirement, superannuation and redundancy payments, s 18(5e) amounts, employment program payments); s 38:
-- weekly earnings exclude prescribed allowances. s 4(1): notional weekly earnings are average weekly earnings, as adjusted
-- under ss 45, 46 or 60, "but not so as to exceed in any case twice State average weekly earnings". s 4(11): "the date on
-- which an incapacity for work first occurs will be taken to be the first day in respect of which the worker has an
-- entitlement to a payment under Part 4 Division 4 Subdivision 2"; (12): the weeks run whether or not the worker is in
-- fact incapacitated throughout.
-- s 42(1): "if the combined amount that a worker would receive in respect of any incapacity for work in any week ... would
-- result in the worker receiving less than the Federal minimum wage (adjusted, in the case of a worker who was working at
-- the relevant date on a part-time basis so as to provide a pro-rata payment), the amount of compensation payable under
-- this Subdivision will be increased so that the combined amount equals the Federal minimum wage". (2)(a): the combined
-- amount is the compensation plus the designated weekly earnings. READING: the s 42 pro-rata adjustment is made as reg 7(2)
-- makes it for s 5(15)(b) (reg 7(2) names only s 5(15)(b)).
DECLARE `Weekly payment facts` HAS
    `paid as a seriously injured worker`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the work capacity`                         IS A `Work capacity`
    `the day incapacity first occurred`          IS A DATE
    `the day asked about`                        IS A DATE
    `notional weekly earnings`                   IS A NUMBER
    `designated weekly earnings`                 IS A NUMBER
    `the Federal minimum wage for the worker`    IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Weekly payment answer` IS ONE OF
    `the weekly payment is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `no weekly payment: not incapacitated for work`
    `no weekly payment: the day is before the incapacity first occurred`
    `no weekly payment: more than 104 weeks after the incapacity first occurred (s 39(3))`
    `no weekly payment: after the worker reached retiring age (s 44(2))`

GIVEN w IS A `Weekly payment facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the full weekly amount for` w MEANS
    CONSIDER w's `the work capacity`
    WHEN `no current work capacity` THEN w's `notional weekly earnings`
    WHEN `a current work capacity` THEN max 0 (w's `notional weekly earnings` MINUS w's `designated weekly earnings`)
    WHEN `not incapacitated for work` THEN 0

-- s 42, applied to an amount payable under s 39, 40 or 41.
GIVEN `the amount` IS A NUMBER, `the designated earnings` IS A NUMBER, `the minimum wage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount` `raised to the s 42 safety net with designated weekly earnings of` `the designated earnings` `and a Federal minimum wage of` `the minimum wage` MEANS
    IF (`the amount` PLUS `the designated earnings`) LESS THAN `the minimum wage`
    THEN `the minimum wage` MINUS `the designated earnings`
    ELSE `the amount`

GIVEN w IS A `Weekly payment facts`
GIVETH A `Weekly payment answer`
`the s 39 or s 41 weekly payment for` w MEANS
    IF `the period` EQUALS 0
    THEN `no weekly payment: the day is before the incapacity first occurred`
    ELSE CONSIDER w's `the work capacity`
         WHEN `not incapacitated for work` THEN `no weekly payment: not incapacitated for work`
         OTHERWISE
             IF `the period` EQUALS 1
             THEN `the weekly payment is` (`safety net` (`the full weekly amount for` w))
             ELSE IF `the period` EQUALS 2 OR w's `paid as a seriously injured worker`
                  THEN `the weekly payment is` (`safety net` (`the full weekly amount for` w TIMES 80%))
                  ELSE `no weekly payment: more than 104 weeks after the incapacity first occurred (s 39(3))`
    WHERE
        `the period` MEANS `the designated period of` (w's `the day asked about`) `counted from` (w's `the day incapacity first occurred`)
        `safety net` x MEANS x `raised to the s 42 safety net with designated weekly earnings of` (w's `designated weekly earnings`) `and a Federal minimum wage of` (w's `the Federal minimum wage for the worker`)

-- s 41(3): a worker paid under s 41 who is "subsequently, on account of an assessment of whole person impairment under
-- this Act, determined not to be a seriously injured worker" keeps the s 41 payments "until the expiration of 8 weeks from
-- the date of the assessment". READING: the 8 weeks are the 56 days from the assessment day, that day counted as day 0.
GIVEN `the day of the assessment` IS A DATE, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day is within 8 weeks of the assessment` `the day of the assessment` `the day` IF
        (`the day of the assessment` `is on or before` `the day`)
    AND `days from` `the day of the assessment` `to` `the day` LESS THAN 56

-- Reg 27: the Federal minimum wage component of s 42 is adjusted each year "(a) if 1 July is a Sunday--on that day; or
-- (b) on the first Sunday following 1 July."
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the s 42 Federal minimum wage is adjusted in` `the year` MEANS
    IF `the weekday of 1 July` EQUALS 0
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 `the year`
    ELSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 `the year`) `plus days` (7 MINUS `the weekday of 1 July`)
    WHERE
        `the weekday of 1 July` MEANS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 `the year`) MODULO 7

§§ `s 40 and reg 26 -- supplementary income support after surgery`

-- s 40(1): "an injured worker who has an incapacity for work as a result of surgery approved by the Corporation is
-- entitled to weekly payments (supplementary income support payments) ... if the incapacity occurs after the end of the
-- second designated period". (2): not "in respect of any period of incapacity that occurs more than 13 weeks after the
-- surgery". (3): payable "at the rate provided by ... section 39(1)(b)" (80%), adjusted under the regulations. Reg 26: the
-- rate is "adjusted to take into account changes in the CPI between the quarter immediately preceding the quarter in which
-- the second designated period came to an end and the quarter falling 2 quarters before the supplementary income support
-- payments commence (with any amount so adjusted being rounded up to the nearest dollar)". The two CPI figures are
-- INPUTS. READING: "more than 13 weeks after" the surgery is more than 91 days after the day of the surgery.
DECLARE `Supplementary facts` HAS
    `the weekly facts`                          IS A `Weekly payment facts`
    `the surgery was approved by the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day of the surgery`                    IS A DATE

DECLARE `Supplementary answer` IS ONE OF
    `the supplementary income support payment is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `no supplementary income support: the day is not after the second designated period`
    `no supplementary income support: the surgery was not approved by the Corporation`
    `no supplementary income support: more than 13 weeks after the surgery`
    `no supplementary income support: not incapacitated for work`

GIVEN s IS A `Supplementary facts`, `the CPI` IS A `CPI figures`
GIVETH A `Supplementary answer`
`the s 40 payment for` s `with` `the CPI` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the designated period of` (w's `the day asked about`) `counted from` (w's `the day incapacity first occurred`) EQUALS 3)
    THEN `no supplementary income support: the day is not after the second designated period`
    ELSE IF NOT s's `the surgery was approved by the Corporation`
         THEN `no supplementary income support: the surgery was not approved by the Corporation`
         ELSE IF `days from` (s's `the day of the surgery`) `to` (w's `the day asked about`) GREATER THAN 91
              THEN `no supplementary income support: more than 13 weeks after the surgery`
              ELSE CONSIDER w's `the work capacity`
                   WHEN `not incapacitated for work` THEN `no supplementary income support: not incapacitated for work`
                   OTHERWISE `the supplementary income support payment is` `the adjusted rate`
    WHERE
        w MEANS s's `the weekly facts`
        `the reg 26 rate` MEANS (`the full weekly amount for` w TIMES (80%)) `indexed by` `the CPI`
        `the adjusted rate` MEANS `the reg 26 rate` `raised to the s 42 safety net with designated weekly earnings of` (w's `designated weekly earnings`) `and a Federal minimum wage of` (w's `the Federal minimum wage for the worker`)

§§ `s 43 -- the worker's return to work obligations`

-- s 43(1): "A worker who has current work capacity must, in cooperation with the employer or Corporation, make reasonable
-- efforts to return to work in suitable employment or pre-injury employment". (2): the worker "is to be treated as making
-- a reasonable effort ... during any reasonable period in which-- (a) the worker is waiting for the commencement of any
-- recovery/return to work services that are required to be provided under a recovery/return to work plan ...; or (b) the
-- worker is waiting for a response to a request for suitable employment or pre-injury employment made by the worker and
-- received by the employer; or (c) if the employer's response is that suitable employment or pre-injury employment will be
-- provided at some time, the worker is waiting for [it] to commence." Whether the period is reasonable is a judgment: an
-- INPUT folded into each fact.
GIVEN `waiting for services under a recovery/return to work plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `waiting for the employer's response to a request for work it received` IS A BOOLEAN
      `waiting for work the employer said it will provide to start` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the worker is treated as making reasonable efforts to return to work` `waiting for services under a recovery/return to work plan` `waiting for the employer's response to a request for work it received` `waiting for work the employer said it will provide to start` IF
        `waiting for services under a recovery/return to work plan`
    OR  `waiting for the employer's response to a request for work it received`
    OR  `waiting for work the employer said it will provide to start`

§§ `s 44 -- weekly payments end at retiring age`

-- s 44(1): "retiring age means-- (a) if there is a normal retiring age for workers in employment of the kind from which the
-- worker's injury arose--that age; or (b) the age at which the worker would, subject to satisfying any other qualifying
-- requirements, be eligible to receive an age pension under the Social Security Act 1991 of the Commonwealth, whichever is
-- the lesser." (2): "Weekly payments are not payable under this Division in respect of a period of incapacity for work
-- falling after the date on which the worker reaches his or her retiring age." (3): "However, if a worker who is within 2
-- years of his or her retiring age or above his or her retiring age becomes incapacitated for work while still in
-- employment, weekly payments are payable for any period of incapacity falling within 104 weeks after the date on which the
-- incapacity for work first occurred". The age pension age is an INPUT (Social Security Act 1991 (Cth) s 23(5A)-(5D)).
-- READING: the 104 weeks of s 44(3) are the same days 0 to 727 as s 39(3).
DECLARE `Retiring age facts` HAS
    `the date of birth`                                           IS A DATE
    `there is a normal retiring age for the kind of employment`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the normal retiring age, in months`                          IS A NUMBER
    `the age pension age, in months`                              IS A NUMBER
    `the day incapacity first occurred`                           IS A DATE
    `still in employment when the incapacity first occurred`      IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN r IS A `Retiring age facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the retiring age in months for` r MEANS
    IF r's `there is a normal retiring age for the kind of employment`
    THEN min (r's `the normal retiring age, in months`) (r's `the age pension age, in months`)
    ELSE r's `the age pension age, in months`

GIVEN r IS A `Retiring age facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the worker reaches retiring age` r MEANS
    `the day a person born on` (r's `the date of birth`) `reaches an age in months of` (`the retiring age in months for` r)

GIVEN r IS A `Retiring age facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 44(3) applies to` r IF
        r's `still in employment when the incapacity first occurred`
    AND ((`the day a person born on` (r's `the date of birth`) `reaches an age in months of` (`the retiring age in months for` r MINUS 24)) `is on or before` (r's `the day incapacity first occurred`))

DECLARE `Retiring age answer` IS ONE OF
    `weekly payments may be paid up to and including` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `no weekly payments: the worker had already reached retiring age and was not in employment`

GIVEN r IS A `Retiring age facts`
GIVETH A `Retiring age answer`
`the s 44 answer for` r MEANS
    IF `s 44(3) applies to` r
    THEN `weekly payments may be paid up to and including` (r's `the day incapacity first occurred` `plus days` 727)
    ELSE IF (`the day the worker reaches retiring age` r) `is on or before` (r's `the day incapacity first occurred` `plus days` (0 MINUS 1))
         THEN `no weekly payments: the worker had already reached retiring age and was not in employment`
         ELSE `weekly payments may be paid up to and including` (`the day the worker reaches retiring age` r)

-- ss 39(3), 41 and 44 together: the last day for which weekly payments can be paid.
GIVEN r IS A `Retiring age facts`, `paid as a seriously injured worker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Retiring age answer`
`the last day of weekly payments for` r `if seriously injured` `paid as a seriously injured worker` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the s 44 answer for` r
    WHEN `weekly payments may be paid up to and including` d THEN
        IF `paid as a seriously injured worker`
        THEN `weekly payments may be paid up to and including` d
        ELSE `weekly payments may be paid up to and including` (`the earlier of` d `and` (r's `the day incapacity first occurred` `plus days` 727))
    OTHERWISE `no weekly payments: the worker had already reached retiring age and was not in employment`

-- The weekly payment on a day, with s 44 applied.
GIVEN w IS A `Weekly payment facts`, r IS A `Retiring age facts`
GIVETH A `Weekly payment answer`
`the weekly payment on the day for` w `with retiring age facts` r MEANS
    CONSIDER `the s 44 answer for` r
    WHEN `weekly payments may be paid up to and including` d THEN
        IF ((w's `the day asked about`) `is on or before` d)
        THEN `the s 39 or s 41 weekly payment for` w
        ELSE IF `the s 39 or s 41 weekly payment for` w EQUALS `no weekly payment: not incapacitated for work`
             THEN `no weekly payment: not incapacitated for work`
             ELSE `no weekly payment: after the worker reached retiring age (s 44(2))`
    OTHERWISE `no weekly payment: after the worker reached retiring age (s 44(2))`

§§ `s 48 and reg 28 -- reducing or discontinuing weekly payments`

-- s 48(1), (2): weekly payments "must not be reduced" or "must not be discontinued" unless a listed ground applies. (5):
-- the Corporation must give the worker written notice with reasons and review rights. (6): "The notice must be given at
-- least the prescribed number of days before the decision is to take effect" where the decision, without the worker's
-- consent, (a) reduces payments because the incapacity has reduced or the overtime would not have continued, (b)
-- discontinues them because the worker has ceased to be incapacitated (but has not returned to work), failed to submit to
-- an examination or provide a certificate, was dismissed for serious and wilful misconduct or breached the obligation of
-- mutuality, or (c) is made under s 46; "in any other case the notice must be given as soon as practicable after the
-- decision is made (but not necessarily before it takes effect)". (7): "the prescribed number of days is-- (a) if the
-- worker's entitlement to weekly payments relates to a period that is within 52 weeks from the date on which incapacity
-- for work first occurred--14 days; (b) in any other case--28 days." (10a): ending an interim s 21(3) decision needs only
-- notice as soon as practicable. READING: (7)(a) is tested on the day the decision is to take effect.
DECLARE `Ground of the decision` IS ONE OF
    `a reduced incapacity, on a health practitioner's certificate, without the worker's consent`
    `overtime the worker would not have continued, without the worker's consent`
    `the worker has ceased to be incapacitated but has not returned to work, without the worker's consent`
    `the worker failed to submit to an examination or to provide a medical certificate`
    `the worker was dismissed for serious and wilful misconduct`
    `the worker breached the obligation of mutuality`
    `a review under s 46`
    `the end of an interim decision that the worker is a seriously injured worker`
    `another ground, such as the worker's consent, a return to work or the passage of time`

DECLARE `Notice period answer` IS ONE OF
    `notice must be given at least this many days before the decision takes effect` HAS `days` IS A NUMBER
    `notice must be given as soon as practicable after the decision, not necessarily before it takes effect`

GIVEN g IS A `Ground of the decision`, `the first day of incapacity` IS A DATE, `the day the decision is to take effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Notice period answer`
`the s 48(6) notice for` g `with incapacity from` `the first day of incapacity` `taking effect on` `the day the decision is to take effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN `the end of an interim decision that the worker is a seriously injured worker` THEN `notice must be given as soon as practicable after the decision, not necessarily before it takes effect`
    WHEN `another ground, such as the worker's consent, a return to work or the passage of time` THEN `notice must be given as soon as practicable after the decision, not necessarily before it takes effect`
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the designated period of` `the day the decision is to take effect` `counted from` `the first day of incapacity` AT MOST 1
        THEN `notice must be given at least this many days before the decision takes effect` 14
        ELSE `notice must be given at least this many days before the decision takes effect` 28

-- s 48(3)-(4): a worker breaches the obligation of mutuality by the refusals and failures listed in (3), "However, a
-- worker does not breach the obligation of mutuality-- (a) by reasonably refusing surgery or the administration of a drug;
-- or (b) where there is a difference of medical opinion about the appropriate treatment ..., or the possibility of choice
-- between a number of reasonable forms of treatment--by choosing 1 form of treatment in preference to another."
DECLARE `Refusal or failure` IS ONE OF
    `reasonably refusing surgery or the administration of a drug`
    `choosing one reasonable form of treatment over another`
    `another refusal or failure listed in s 48(3)`
    `none`

GIVEN r IS A `Refusal or failure`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the worker breaches the obligation of mutuality by` r IF
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `another refusal or failure listed in s 48(3)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 48(11), (12): if a dispute is resolved for the worker, the arrears are paid, "increased by interest at the prescribed
-- rate". Reg 28(1): "the amount in arrears will be increased by interest on the amount at the prime bank rate for the
-- financial year in which the amount went into arrears, compounded on a weekly basis for each complete week that the
-- amount is in arrears." Reg 3: the prime bank rate is an average of two NAB rates at the start of the financial year:
-- an INPUT. READING: the weekly rate is the annual rate divided by 52. Reg 28(2) (arrears across financial years, each at
-- its own rate) is met by working each year's arrears separately.
GIVEN `the arrears` IS A NUMBER, `the prime bank rate in per cent` IS A NUMBER, `the complete weeks in arrears` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the arrears` `with reg 28 interest at` `the prime bank rate in per cent` `for` `the complete weeks in arrears` MEANS
    `the arrears` TIMES (`power` (1 PLUS (`the prime bank rate in per cent` DIVIDED BY 100 DIVIDED BY 52)) `the complete weeks in arrears`)

§§ `ss 55, 56 and Schedules 6, 7 -- the lump sum for economic loss`

-- Schedule 6 (age factor), "Worker's age at the relevant date (in years)", from "25 or less|100%" to "70 or more|0%". The
-- row below is ages 25 to 70.
`the Schedule 6 percentages for ages 25 to 70` MEANS
    LIST 100, 99, 98, 97, 96, 95, 94, 93, 92, 91, 90, 89, 88, 87, 86, 85, 84, 83, 82, 81, 80,
         78, 76, 74, 72, 70, 68, 66, 64, 62, 60,
         56, 52, 48, 44, 40, 36, 32, 28, 24, 20, 16, 12, 8, 4, 0

-- s 55(2), (3): "the age factor is the percentage that applies ... under Schedule 6", by "the worker's age at the relevant
-- date" (the day of the injury, s 5(16)(a)).
GIVEN `the age in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the age factor in per cent at age` `the age in years` MEANS
    IF `the age in years` AT MOST 25
    THEN 100
    ELSE IF `the age in years` AT LEAST 70
         THEN 0
         ELSE `entry` (`the age in years` MINUS 24) `of` `the Schedule 6 percentages for ages 25 to 70`

-- Schedule 7 (prescribed sum, economic loss), "5%|$5 000 (indexed)" to "34% or more|$434 863 (indexed)". s 55(8): "the
-- prescribed sum is the amount applying under Schedule 7 in relation to a worker's whole person impairment"; (9): "the
-- amount applying under Schedule 7 at the relevant date". Schedule 7 was amended by the 2022 amending Act (s 19), which
-- applies only where the final examination was on or after the designated day (Schedule 1 clause 2 of that Act).
`the Schedule 7 sums for 5% to 34%` MEANS
    LIST 5000, 7785, 12027, 20296, 30067, 41342, 48437, 56105, 63572, 73512,
         86453, 95574, 106178, 120643, 135731, 153296, 168781, 186285, 204170, 222389,
         242659, 263215, 290602, 318645, 350000, 371723, 386592, 402056, 418138, 434863

GIVEN `the whole person impairment in per cent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Schedule 7 stated sum for` `the whole person impairment in per cent` MEANS
    IF `the whole person impairment in per cent` LESS THAN 5
    THEN 0
    ELSE `entry` ((min `the whole person impairment in per cent` 34) MINUS 4) `of` `the Schedule 7 sums for 5% to 34%`

-- s 55(4): "the hours worked factor is the number of hours per week being worked by the worker (whether full-time or
-- part-time) at the relevant date, expressed as a percentage of full-time work". (7): a part-time worker with a legally
-- enforceable right to return to full-time work is taken as full-time (the caller gives full-time hours).
GIVEN `the weekly hours` IS A NUMBER, `the hours of full-time work` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the hours worked factor in per cent for` `the weekly hours` `of` `the hours of full-time work` MEANS
    `the weekly hours` DIVIDED BY `the hours of full-time work` TIMES 100

-- s 56(1): "if a worker, other than a prescribed seriously injured worker, suffers a work injury resulting in permanent
-- impairment ..., the worker is entitled ... to compensation for loss of future earning capacity by way of a lump sum."
-- (12): "prescribed seriously injured worker means a seriously injured worker who has not made an election under section
-- 56A." (2): no entitlement "if the worker's degree of whole person impairment from physical injury is less than 5%".
-- (3): none for "(a) a psychiatric injury or consequential mental harm; or (b) noise induced hearing loss". (10): "not
-- payable ... after the death of the worker". (4): "the lump sum will be an amount determined as follows:" -- the
-- FORMULA IS MISSING from the deposit; its terms are LS, PS (the prescribed sum, "cannot exceed the prescribed sum
-- applicable for 34% whole person impairment"), AF (age factor) and HWF (hours worked factor). So the lump sum answers
-- `not covered`. (11): "in no case can the lump sum exceed the prescribed sum adjusted by the age factor": that ceiling
-- is given.
DECLARE `Economic loss facts` HAS
    `a seriously injured worker`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `made an election under s 56A`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the whole person impairment from physical injury, in per cent` IS A NUMBER
    `the injury is noise induced hearing loss`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the worker has died`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the final examination was on or after the 2022 designated day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the age in years at the day of the injury`                    IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Economic loss answer` IS ONE OF
    `not covered: the s 56(4) formula is missing from the deposited text; s 56(11) caps the lump sum at` HAS `the ceiling` IS A NUMBER
    `no lump sum for economic loss: a seriously injured worker who has not elected under s 56A (s 56(1), (12))`
    `no lump sum for economic loss: physical impairment under 5% (s 56(2))`
    `no lump sum for economic loss: noise induced hearing loss (s 56(3)(b))`
    `no lump sum for economic loss: the worker has died (s 56(10))`
    `not covered: the Schedule 7 sums for a final examination before the 2022 designated day are not in the deposited text`
    `not covered: Schedule 7 has no row for a whole person impairment that is not a whole number`

GIVEN e IS AN `Economic loss facts`, `the CPI` IS A `CPI figures`
GIVETH AN `Economic loss answer`
`the s 56 answer for` e `with` `the CPI` MEANS
    IF e's `a seriously injured worker` AND (NOT e's `made an election under s 56A`)
    THEN `no lump sum for economic loss: a seriously injured worker who has not elected under s 56A (s 56(1), (12))`
    ELSE IF e's `the worker has died`
         THEN `no lump sum for economic loss: the worker has died (s 56(10))`
         ELSE IF e's `the injury is noise induced hearing loss`
              THEN `no lump sum for economic loss: noise induced hearing loss (s 56(3)(b))`
              ELSE IF `the WPI` LESS THAN 5
                   THEN `no lump sum for economic loss: physical impairment under 5% (s 56(2))`
                   ELSE IF NOT e's `the final examination was on or after the 2022 designated day`
                        THEN `not covered: the Schedule 7 sums for a final examination before the 2022 designated day are not in the deposited text`
                        ELSE IF NOT (`is a whole number` `the WPI`)
                             THEN `not covered: Schedule 7 has no row for a whole person impairment that is not a whole number`
                             ELSE `not covered: the s 56(4) formula is missing from the deposited text; s 56(11) caps the lump sum at`
                                      (((`the Schedule 7 stated sum for` `the WPI`) `indexed by` `the CPI`) TIMES (`the age factor in per cent at age` (e's `the age in years at the day of the injury`)) DIVIDED BY 100)
    WHERE
        `the WPI` MEANS e's `the whole person impairment from physical injury, in per cent`

§§ `ss 57, 58, reg 34 and Schedule 1 of the regulations -- the lump sum for non-economic loss`

-- s 57(1): "the prescribed sum is-- (a) unless a regulation has been made under paragraph (b)--$472 000 (indexed)"; (2)(a):
-- "the amount to be applied with respect to a particular injury is the amount applying ... at the time of the occurrence of
-- that injury". No regulation under s 57(1)(b) is in the deposited regulations.
`the s 57 prescribed sum, as stated` MEANS 472000

-- Regulations, Schedule 1 (reg 34(1)): "WPI degree|Compensation amount", 0 to 4: 0; 5: $12 051 (indexed) ... 49: $462 321
-- (indexed); 50 to 100: $482 014 (indexed), the same in every row. Reg 34(2): "the amount applying at the time of the
-- occurrence of the injury".
`the regulation Schedule 1 amounts for 5 to 49` MEANS
    LIST 12051, 13766, 15513, 17351, 19281, 21209, 23131, 25225, 27475, 29885,
         32295, 34824, 37598, 40490, 43555, 46895, 51764, 57506, 63500, 69744,
         76802, 84141, 92356, 100885, 109729, 120165, 130323, 141498, 153735, 166382,
         179438, 193635, 209022, 224880, 241991, 259604, 277720, 297166, 317991, 339381,
         362212, 385640, 409665, 435210, 462321

`the regulation Schedule 1 amount for 50 to 100` MEANS 482014

GIVEN `the WPI degree` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the regulation Schedule 1 stated amount for` `the WPI degree` MEANS
    IF `the WPI degree` LESS THAN 5
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the WPI degree` AT LEAST 50
         THEN `the regulation Schedule 1 amount for 50 to 100`
         ELSE `entry` (`the WPI degree` MINUS 4) `of` `the regulation Schedule 1 amounts for 5 to 49`

-- Schedule 8 of the Act: the regulations must pay at least "5% - 9% (inclusive)|$11 800 (indexed)", "10% - 29%|$20 768",
-- "30% - 49%|$117 668", "50% - 100%|$472 000" (s 58(5)).
GIVEN `the WPI degree` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Schedule 8 minimum, as stated, for` `the WPI degree` MEANS
    IF `the WPI degree` LESS THAN 5
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the WPI degree` AT MOST 9
         THEN 11800
         ELSE IF `the WPI degree` AT MOST 29
              THEN 20768
              ELSE IF `the WPI degree` AT MOST 49
                   THEN 117668
                   ELSE 472000

-- s 58(1): a worker whose work injury results in permanent impairment "is entitled ... to compensation for non-economic loss
-- by way of a lump sum". (2): none "if the worker's degree of whole person impairment from physical injury is less than
-- 5%"; (3): none "in relation to a psychiatric injury or consequential mental harm"; (4): "a portion of the prescribed sum
-- calculated in accordance with the regulations"; (6): for "2 or more impairments arising from the same injury or cause"
-- the worker "is not entitled to receive compensation ... in excess of the prescribed sum"; (7): an aggravation of a prior
-- work injury is reduced "by the amount of the previous payment"; (11): "not payable ... after the death of the worker".
-- Both sums are indexed from the September quarter of 2014 (reg 4; s 4(17) with s 57 commencing on 1 July 2015, per the
-- deposit's legislative history), so one pair of CPI figures serves both (finding 13).
DECLARE `Non-economic loss facts` HAS
    `the whole person impairment from physical injury, in per cent` IS A NUMBER
    `the worker has died`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `two or more impairments from the same injury or cause were combined` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the injury aggravates a prior work injury already paid for under s 58` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the previous s 58 payment`                                    IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Non-economic loss answer` IS ONE OF
    `the lump sum for non-economic loss is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `no lump sum for non-economic loss: physical impairment under 5% (s 58(2), (3))`
    `no lump sum for non-economic loss: the worker has died (s 58(11))`
    `not covered: the regulation Schedule 1 scale has no row for a whole person impairment that is not a whole number`

GIVEN n IS A `Non-economic loss facts`, `the CPI` IS A `CPI figures`
GIVETH A `Non-economic loss answer`
`the s 58 answer for` n `with` `the CPI` MEANS
    IF n's `the worker has died`
    THEN `no lump sum for non-economic loss: the worker has died (s 58(11))`
    ELSE IF `the WPI` LESS THAN 5
         THEN `no lump sum for non-economic loss: physical impairment under 5% (s 58(2), (3))`
         ELSE IF NOT (`is a whole number` `the WPI`)
              THEN `not covered: the regulation Schedule 1 scale has no row for a whole person impairment that is not a whole number`
              ELSE `the lump sum for non-economic loss is` `after the reduction`
    WHERE
        `the WPI` MEANS n's `the whole person impairment from physical injury, in per cent`
        `the scale amount` MEANS (`the regulation Schedule 1 stated amount for` `the WPI`) `indexed by` `the CPI`
        `after the cap` MEANS
            IF n's `two or more impairments from the same injury or cause were combined`
            THEN min `the scale amount` (`the s 57 prescribed sum, as stated` `indexed by` `the CPI`)
            ELSE `the scale amount`
        `after the reduction` MEANS
            IF n's `the injury aggravates a prior work injury already paid for under s 58`
            THEN max 0 (`after the cap` MINUS n's `the previous s 58 payment`)
            ELSE `after the cap`

§§ `ss 59, 61, 62 and reg 35 -- payments on death`

-- s 59(1): weekly payments on a worker's death from a work injury: "(a) a dependent spouse or domestic partner ...-- (i)
-- in the case of total dependency--50%"; "(b) a dependent child (being an orphaned child) ...--25%"; "(c) a dependent
-- child (not being an orphaned child) ...--12.5%", each "of the amount of the notional weekly earnings of the deceased
-- worker"; partial dependency at "such lesser percentage as may be fixed by the Corporation" and (d) other dependent
-- relatives at an amount "determined by the Corporation" (INPUTS).
-- (5): "Weekly payments will not be made to a dependent child ... unless-- (a) the child is under the age of 18 years; or
-- (b) the child is a full-time student at an educational institution approved by the Corporation ... and is under the age
-- of 26 years; or (c) the child is, by reason of disability, incapable of earning a living." s 61(1) defines "child" in
-- the same three ways.
-- (6): not "beyond the date at which such payments would, assuming that the worker had survived but had been a seriously
-- injured worker, have ceased to be payable to the worker" (s 44, with s 41). (7): if the payments "would ... exceed in
-- aggregate the amount of the weekly payments to which the worker would have been entitled in the event of being a
-- seriously injured worker with no current work capacity, the weekly payments must be proportionately reduced": that is
-- the notional weekly earnings in the first 52 weeks from the first incapacity, 80% after (s 41(1)).
GIVEN `the age in years` IS A NUMBER, `a full-time student at an approved institution` IS A BOOLEAN, `incapable of earning a living by reason of disability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a child of` `the age in years` `may be paid` `a full-time student at an approved institution` `incapable of earning a living by reason of disability` IF
        `the age in years` LESS THAN 18
    OR  (`a full-time student at an approved institution` AND `the age in years` LESS THAN 26)
    OR  `incapable of earning a living by reason of disability`

GIVEN `the shares in per cent of notional weekly earnings` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the notional earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `within 52 weeks of the first incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the s 59 weekly payments for shares` `the shares in per cent of notional weekly earnings` `of` `the notional earnings` `within the first 52 weeks` `within 52 weeks of the first incapacity` MEANS
    map (GIVEN s YIELD s DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES `the notional earnings` TIMES `the reduction`) `the shares in per cent of notional weekly earnings`
    WHERE
        `the total share` MEANS sum `the shares in per cent of notional weekly earnings`
        `the cap share` MEANS IF `within 52 weeks of the first incapacity` THEN 100 ELSE 80
        `the reduction` MEANS
            IF `the total share` GREATER THAN `the cap share`
            THEN `the cap share` DIVIDED BY `the total share`
            ELSE 1

-- s 61(1): "prescribed sum means the prescribed sum applying under Division 7 (as at the time of the occurrence of the work
-- injury that resulted in the death of the relevant worker) but less any amount paid to the relevant worker under Division
-- 7". "partner means a spouse or domestic partner". (3) partners and no child: the sum in equal shares to the partners.
-- (4) children and no partner: the sum in equal shares to the children. (5) partners and "1 (and only 1) child": "90% of
-- the prescribed sum" to the partners in equal shares, "10% of the prescribed sum payable to the child". (6) partners and
-- "more than 1 and not more than 5 children": "5% of the prescribed sum payable to each child" and "the balance to the
-- partner" (in equal shares). (7) partners and "more than 5 children": 75% to the partners, 25% to the children, each in
-- equal shares. (8) no partner or child: the Corporation "may ... pay compensation not exceeding the prescribed sum" to
-- a person dependent on the worker's earnings. Neither "partner" nor "child" in s 61 requires dependency (finding 14).
DECLARE `Death lump sum answer` IS ONE OF
    `each partner's share and each child's share are` HAS `each partner's share` IS A NUMBER, `each child's share` IS A NUMBER
    `no partner or child: the Corporation may pay dependants up to, in all,` HAS `the prescribed sum` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the number of partners` IS A NUMBER, `the number of children` IS A NUMBER, `the sum to share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Death lump sum answer`
`the s 61 shares for` `the number of partners` `partners and` `the number of children` `children of` `the sum to share` MEANS
    IF `the number of partners` EQUALS 0
    THEN IF `the number of children` EQUALS 0
         THEN `no partner or child: the Corporation may pay dependants up to, in all,` `the sum to share`
         ELSE `each partner's share and each child's share are` 0 (`the sum to share` DIVIDED BY `the number of children`)
    ELSE IF `the number of children` EQUALS 0
         THEN `each partner's share and each child's share are` (`the sum to share` DIVIDED BY `the number of partners`) 0
         ELSE IF `the number of children` EQUALS 1
              THEN `each partner's share and each child's share are` (`the sum to share` TIMES 90% DIVIDED BY `the number of partners`) (`the sum to share` TIMES 10%)
              ELSE IF `the number of children` AT MOST 5
                   THEN `each partner's share and each child's share are` ((`the sum to share` MINUS (`the sum to share` TIMES 5% TIMES `the number of children`)) DIVIDED BY `the number of partners`) (`the sum to share` TIMES 5%)
                   ELSE `each partner's share and each child's share are` (`the sum to share` TIMES 75% DIVIDED BY `the number of partners`) (`the sum to share` TIMES 25% DIVIDED BY `the number of children`)

GIVEN `the paid amount under Division 7` IS A NUMBER, `the CPI` IS A `CPI figures`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 61 prescribed sum, less` `the paid amount under Division 7` `with` `the CPI` MEANS
    max 0 ((`the s 57 prescribed sum, as stated` `indexed by` `the CPI`) MINUS `the paid amount under Division 7`)

-- s 61(11): "A claimant is entitled to interest at the prescribed rate on an amount of compensation payable under this
-- section in respect of the period beginning on the date the claim for compensation was lodged ... and ending on the date
-- of the payment." Reg 35(2): "the prime bank rate for the financial year in which the compensation is paid" (an INPUT).
-- READING: simple interest, by days over a 365-day year; reg 35(2), unlike reg 28, says nothing of compounding.
GIVEN `the amount` IS A NUMBER, `the prime bank rate in per cent` IS A NUMBER, `the day the claim was lodged` IS A DATE, `the day of payment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 61(11) interest on` `the amount` `at` `the prime bank rate in per cent` `from` `the day the claim was lodged` `to` `the day of payment` MEANS
    `the amount` TIMES `the prime bank rate in per cent` DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES (`days from` `the day the claim was lodged` `to` `the day of payment`) DIVIDED BY 365

-- s 62(1): "a funeral benefit is payable equal to-- (a) the actual cost of the worker's funeral; or (b) the prescribed
-- amount, whichever is the lesser"; (2): paid to the person who conducted the funeral, or who paid or is liable to pay its
-- expenses. Reg 35(3): "$10 172 (indexed)".
GIVEN `the actual cost of the funeral` IS A NUMBER, `the CPI` IS A `CPI figures`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the funeral benefit for a funeral costing` `the actual cost of the funeral` `with` `the CPI` MEANS
    min `the actual cost of the funeral` (10172 `indexed by` `the CPI`)

§§ `s 72 -- damages against the employer`

-- s 72(1): "No damages may be awarded against an employer ... unless the injury results in-- (a) in the case of physical
-- injury--a degree of permanent impairment of the worker that is at least 35%; or (b) in the case of psychiatric
-- injury--... at least 30%; or (c) the death of the worker." (3): physical and psychiatric impairment are assessed
-- separately. s 72(1) as substituted by the 2022 amending Act applies to a physical injury only where the final
-- examination was on or after the designated day (Schedule 1 clause 2 of that Act).
DECLARE `Damages answer` IS ONE OF
    `damages may be awarded against the employer, if the general law gives them (s 72(1))`
    `no damages may be awarded against the employer (s 72(1))`
    `not covered: the s 72 threshold for a physical injury whose final examination was before the 2022 designated day is not in the deposited text`

GIVEN p IS AN `Impairment facts`, `the worker died of the injury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Damages answer`
`the s 72 answer for` p `with death` `the worker died of the injury` MEANS
    IF `the worker died of the injury` OR p's `the whole person impairment from psychiatric injury, in per cent` AT LEAST 30
    THEN `damages may be awarded against the employer, if the general law gives them (s 72(1))`
    ELSE IF (NOT p's `the final examination was on or after the 2022 designated day`) AND p's `the whole person impairment from physical injury, in per cent` GREATER THAN 0
         THEN `not covered: the s 72 threshold for a physical injury whose final examination was before the 2022 designated day is not in the deposited text`
         ELSE IF p's `the whole person impairment from physical injury, in per cent` AT LEAST 35
              THEN `damages may be awarded against the employer, if the general law gives them (s 72(1))`
              ELSE `no damages may be awarded against the employer (s 72(1))`

§§ `s 100 -- time to apply to the Tribunal`

-- s 100: "(1) An application may be made to the Tribunal within 1 month after the applicant receives notice of the
-- reviewable decision unless the Tribunal allows an extension of time. (2) The Tribunal must only allow an extension of
-- time under subsection (1) if satisfied-- (a) that good reason exists; and (b) that another party will not be
-- unreasonably disadvantaged because of the delay". The Tribunal's satisfaction is an INPUT.
GIVEN `the day notice of the decision was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply to the Tribunal after notice received on` `the day notice of the decision was received` MEANS
    `the day notice of the decision was received` `plus months` 1

GIVEN `the Tribunal is satisfied good reason exists` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Tribunal is satisfied no other party is unreasonably disadvantaged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Tribunal may extend the time` `the Tribunal is satisfied good reason exists` `the Tribunal is satisfied no other party is unreasonably disadvantaged` IF
    `the Tribunal is satisfied good reason exists` AND `the Tribunal is satisfied no other party is unreasonably disadvantaged`

§§ `s 18 and reg 12 -- the employer's duty to provide work`

-- s 18(1): "If a worker who has been incapacitated for work in consequence of a work injury is able to return to work
-- (whether on a full-time or part-time basis and whether or not to his or her previous employment), including if the
-- worker has ceased to be incapacitated ..., the employer from whose employment the injury arose (the pre-injury employer)
-- must provide suitable employment for the worker". (2): "Subsection (1) does not apply if-- (a) it is not reasonably
-- practicable to provide employment ... (and the onus of establishing that lies on the employer); or (b) the worker left
-- the employment of that employer before the commencement of the incapacity for work; or (c) the worker terminated the
-- employment after the commencement of the incapacity for work; or (ca) the worker's employment ... has been properly
-- terminated on the ground of serious and wilful misconduct (and the onus of establishing that lies on the employer); or
-- (d) new or other employment options have been agreed to by the worker under section 25(10a); or (e) the worker has
-- otherwise returned to work with the pre-injury employer or another employer." Whether the employer has established (a)
-- or (ca) is decided by others: INPUTS.
DECLARE `Suitable work facts` HAS
    `the worker was incapacitated for work by a work injury from this employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the worker is able to return to work`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer has established it is not reasonably practicable`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the worker left this employer before the incapacity began`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the worker ended the employment after the incapacity began`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer has established a proper termination for serious and wilful misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the worker agreed to other employment options under s 25(10a)`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the worker has otherwise returned to work`                               IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN s IS A `Suitable work facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the pre-injury employer must provide suitable employment` s IF
        s's `the worker was incapacitated for work by a work injury from this employment`
    AND s's `the worker is able to return to work`
    AND (NOT s's `the employer has established it is not reasonably practicable`)
    AND (NOT s's `the worker left this employer before the incapacity began`)
    AND (NOT s's `the worker ended the employment after the incapacity began`)
    AND (NOT s's `the employer has established a proper termination for serious and wilful misconduct`)
    AND (NOT s's `the worker agreed to other employment options under s 25(10a)`)
    AND (NOT s's `the worker has otherwise returned to work`)

-- s 18(3): the worker who seeks the employment "must ... (a) give written notice to the employer (a subsection (3)
-- notice)-- (i) confirming that they are ready, willing and able to return to work with the employer; and (ii) providing
-- information about the type of employment that the worker considers that they are capable of performing; and (iii) [for
-- a labour hire worker who seeks the host employer's cooperation] containing a statement to that effect". (4): "A
-- subsection (3) notice must be supported by evidence of the worker's capacity for work."
GIVEN `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `confirms the worker is ready, willing and able to return to work with the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `describes the type of employment the worker considers they can perform` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a labour hire worker seeking the host employer's cooperation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `contains a statement seeking the host employer's cooperation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `supported by evidence of capacity for work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice is a subsection (3) notice` `in writing` `confirms the worker is ready, willing and able to return to work with the employer` `describes the type of employment the worker considers they can perform` `a labour hire worker seeking the host employer's cooperation` `contains a statement seeking the host employer's cooperation` `supported by evidence of capacity for work` IF
        `in writing`
    AND `confirms the worker is ready, willing and able to return to work with the employer`
    AND `describes the type of employment the worker considers they can perform`
    AND ((NOT `a labour hire worker seeking the host employer's cooperation`) OR `contains a statement seeking the host employer's cooperation`)
    AND `supported by evidence of capacity for work`

-- s 18(4b): "The pre-injury employer must, within 1 month of receiving a subsection (3) notice from a worker, notify the
-- worker in writing whether they will provide the worker-- (a) with suitable employment of the type the worker considers
-- that they are capable of performing ...; or (b) with other suitable employment". (4c): grounds for a refusal; reasons for
-- other employment. (4d): if the employer "refuses or otherwise fails to provide suitable employment ..., or the worker
-- considers that any employment offered ... under subsection (4b)(b) is not suitable, the worker may apply to the Tribunal
-- for an order under subsection (5)-- (a) within 1 month after the date on which the pre-injury employer provided written
-- notice under subsection (4b); or (b) if the pre-injury employer failed to provide written notice under subsection
-- (4b)--within 1 month after the end of the 1 month period in which the employer was required to give the notice". (4e):
-- the worker cannot apply "if, at the time of giving a subsection (3) notice to the employer, the worker had ceased to be
-- incapacitated for work in consequence of the work injury and did not give that notice within 6 months of ceasing to be
-- incapacitated". READING: the month in (4d)(b) is added to the end of the first month, not 2 months to the day of receipt.
GIVEN `the day of receipt` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the employer's written reply to a notice received on` `the day of receipt` MEANS
    `the day of receipt` `plus months` 1

DECLARE `Tribunal window answer` IS ONE OF
    `the worker may apply to the Tribunal no later than` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `the worker cannot apply to the Tribunal under s 18(4d): s 18(4e)`

DECLARE `Subsection (3) timing facts` HAS
    `the day the employer received the subsection (3) notice`            IS A DATE
    `the employer gave a written reply`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day of the employer's written reply`                            IS A DATE
    `the worker had ceased to be incapacitated when giving the notice`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the worker ceased to be incapacitated`                      IS A DATE

GIVEN t IS A `Subsection (3) timing facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18(4e) bars an application to the Tribunal for` t IF
        t's `the worker had ceased to be incapacitated when giving the notice`
    AND (NOT (t's `the day the employer received the subsection (3) notice` `is on or before` (t's `the day the worker ceased to be incapacitated` `plus months` 6)))

GIVEN t IS A `Subsection (3) timing facts`
GIVETH A `Tribunal window answer`
`the s 18(4d) window for` t MEANS
    IF `s 18(4e) bars an application to the Tribunal for` t
    THEN `the worker cannot apply to the Tribunal under s 18(4d): s 18(4e)`
    ELSE IF t's `the employer gave a written reply`
         THEN `the worker may apply to the Tribunal no later than` (t's `the day of the employer's written reply` `plus months` 1)
         ELSE `the worker may apply to the Tribunal no later than` ((`the last day for the employer's written reply to a notice received on` (t's `the day the employer received the subsection (3) notice`)) `plus months` 1)

-- Reg 12(1): "For the purposes of section 18(6) of the Act, the following limits on costs (excluding reasonably incurred
-- disbursements such as counsel fees) awarded to a party who is represented ... are prescribed: (a) for assistance in the
-- preparation and lodgement of an application to the Tribunal under section 18(3) of the Act--$402 (indexed); (b) for
-- participation in proceedings ... (up to and including a pre-hearing conference ...)-- (i) $745 (indexed); or (ii) if
-- the Tribunal determines ... that the party is entitled to an award of costs of an amount greater than $745
-- (indexed)--$2 464 (indexed); (c) for proceedings ... after a pre-hearing conference ...--85% of the amount that would be
-- allowable under the relevant Supreme Court scale". The Supreme Court scale amount is an INPUT. Reg 12 still refers to
-- "an application to the Tribunal under section 18(3)", which since 1 December 2024 is the worker's notice to the employer
-- (finding 7).
DECLARE `Stage of the s 18 proceedings` IS ONE OF
    `preparing and lodging the application`
    `taking part up to and including a pre-hearing conference`
    `taking part up to a pre-hearing conference, where the Tribunal determines a greater amount`
    `proceedings after a pre-hearing conference`

GIVEN `the stage` IS A `Stage of the s 18 proceedings`, `the Supreme Court scale amount` IS A NUMBER, `the CPI` IS A `CPI figures`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the reg 12 costs limit for` `the stage` `with a Supreme Court scale amount of` `the Supreme Court scale amount` `and` `the CPI` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the stage`
    WHEN `preparing and lodging the application` THEN 402 `indexed by` `the CPI`
    WHEN `taking part up to and including a pre-hearing conference` THEN 745 `indexed by` `the CPI`
    WHEN `taking part up to a pre-hearing conference, where the Tribunal determines a greater amount` THEN 2464 `indexed by` `the CPI`
    WHEN `proceedings after a pre-hearing conference` THEN `the Supreme Court scale amount` TIMES 85%

§§ `s 20 -- terminating the employment of an injured worker`

-- s 20(1): "If a worker has suffered a work injury, the employer from whose employment the injury arose must not terminate
-- the worker's employment without first giving the Corporation and the worker at least 28 days notice of the proposed
-- termination." (2): "However, notice of termination is not required under this section if-- (a) the employment is
-- properly terminated on the ground of serious and wilful misconduct; or (b) the worker is neither participating in a
-- recovery/return to work plan, nor receiving compensation, for the work injury; or (c) the worker's rights to
-- compensation for the injury have been exhausted or the time for making a claim for compensation has expired." (3): the
-- employer bears the burden of establishing serious and wilful misconduct. No penalty is stated.
DECLARE `Termination facts` HAS
    `the worker suffered a work injury in this employment`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `a proper termination for serious and wilful misconduct, established by the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the worker is in a recovery/return to work plan or receiving compensation for the injury` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the worker's rights to compensation are exhausted or the time to claim has expired` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN t IS A `Termination facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 20 notice is required before terminating` t IF
        t's `the worker suffered a work injury in this employment`
    AND (NOT t's `a proper termination for serious and wilful misconduct, established by the employer`)
    AND t's `the worker is in a recovery/return to work plan or receiving compensation for the injury`
    AND (NOT t's `the worker's rights to compensation are exhausted or the time to claim has expired`)

-- READING: "at least 28 days notice" -- the employment may end on the 28th day after the day notice is given.
GIVEN `the day notice was given to the worker and the Corporation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earliest day the employment may end after notice on` `the day notice was given to the worker and the Corporation` MEANS
    `the day notice was given to the worker and the Corporation` `plus days` 28

§§ `Regulative rules -- the worker, the employer and the Corporation`

-- Clock: days, counted from the day the rule starts (named in each rule), except the s 16 rule, which counts hours from
-- the injury. Business-day and month periods are given to a rule as the calendar days they span in that case (worked out
-- with rtw-dates.l4). A rule under LEST starts when the trace first notices that the deadline has passed: at the next
-- event or WAITUNTIL.
DECLARE `RTW party` IS ONE OF `the worker`, `the employer`, `the Corporation`

DECLARE `Written reply` IS ONE OF
    `it will provide suitable employment of the type the worker nominated`
    `it will provide other suitable employment, with its reasons`
    `it refuses, with its grounds`

DECLARE `RTW act` IS ONE OF
    `give notice of the injury`
    `send the Corporation a copy of the notice of injury`
    `give the claim`
    `forward a copy of the claim and a statement in the designated form to the Corporation`
    `furnish the information the Corporation reasonably requires`
    `determine the claim`
    `offer to make interim payments`
    `provide suitable employment`
    `notify the worker in writing` HAS `the reply` IS A `Written reply`
    `apply to the Tribunal for an order to provide employment`
    `terminate the worker's employment`
    `make reasonable efforts to return to work`
    `apply to the Tribunal for review and elect that weekly payments continue`
    `continue or reinstate the weekly payments`

-- s 16(1), (2), from the injury, in HOURS. The 24 hours (or what was practicable) are what notice "should" meet; the duty
-- in s 16(1) is that notice "must be given". So a late notice still satisfies s 16(1), and missing the hours is not a
-- breach: the duty simply remains, and until notice is given s 30(2) stops a claim being made (unless s 30(3)(a) excuses
-- the want of notice). Finding 3.
GIVEN `the hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `RTW party` `RTW act`
DECIDE `s 16(1), (2) -- the worker must give notice of the injury, within 24 hours if practicable` `the hours` IS
    PARTY `the worker`
    MUST  `give notice of the injury`
    WITHIN `the hours`
    LEST
        PARTY `the worker`
        MUST  `give notice of the injury`

-- s 16(6), from the day the employer receives the notice.
GIVEN `self-insured` IS A BOOLEAN, `the calendar days to the 5th business day after receipt` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `RTW party` `RTW act`
DECIDE `s 16(6) -- the employer must send the Corporation a copy of the notice within 5 business days` `self-insured` `the calendar days to the 5th business day after receipt` IS
    IF `self-insured`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the employer`
         MUST  `send the Corporation a copy of the notice of injury`
         WITHIN `the calendar days to the 5th business day after receipt`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "s 16(6): an employer that is not self-insured must send the Corporation a copy of the notice of injury within 5 business days after receiving it; maximum penalty $1 500"

-- s 30(5), from the day the employer receives the claim.
GIVEN `given to the employer` IS A BOOLEAN, `self-insured` IS A BOOLEAN, `the calendar days to the 5th business day after receipt` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `RTW party` `RTW act`
`s 30(5) -- once the claim is given` `given to the employer` `self-insured` `the calendar days to the 5th business day after receipt` MEANS
    IF `given to the employer` AND (NOT `self-insured`)
    THEN PARTY `the employer`
         MUST  `forward a copy of the claim and a statement in the designated form to the Corporation`
         WITHIN `the calendar days to the 5th business day after receipt`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "s 30(5): an employer that is not self-insured must forward a copy of the claim and a statement in the designated form to the Corporation within 5 business days after receiving it; maximum penalty $1 500"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 30(1)(b), (3)(b), (10), from the day the entitlement to make the claim arises. Making a claim is the worker's choice
-- (DO); the 6 months are a condition of it. After the 6 months a late claim may still be made if s 30(3)(b) excuses it;
-- otherwise the trace ends in BREACH, which here marks the time bar, not an offence.
DECLARE `Claim rule facts` HAS
    `the calendar days in the prescribed period`                        IS A NUMBER
    `the claim is given to the employer`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer is self-insured`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 30(3)(b) excuses a late claim`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the calendar days to the 5th business day after the employer receives the claim` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN c IS A `Claim rule facts`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `RTW party` `RTW act`
`s 30(3)(b) -- after the prescribed period` c MEANS
    IF c's `s 30(3)(b) excuses a late claim`
    THEN PARTY `the worker`
         DO    `give the claim`
         HENCE `s 30(5) -- once the claim is given` (c's `the claim is given to the employer`) (c's `the employer is self-insured`) (c's `the calendar days to the 5th business day after the employer receives the claim`)
    ELSE BREACH BY `the worker` BECAUSE "s 30(1)(b), (10): the claim was not made within 6 months of the day the entitlement arose, and s 30(3)(b) does not excuse the delay; the claim is barred"

GIVEN c IS A `Claim rule facts`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `RTW party` `RTW act`
DECIDE `s 30(1), (3)(b), (5) -- a claim within 6 months, forwarded by the employer within 5 business days` c IS
    PARTY `the worker`
    DO    `give the claim`
    WITHIN c's `the calendar days in the prescribed period`
    HENCE `s 30(5) -- once the claim is given` (c's `the claim is given to the employer`) (c's `the employer is self-insured`) (c's `the calendar days to the 5th business day after the employer receives the claim`)
    LEST  `s 30(3)(b) -- after the prescribed period` c

-- s 30(6), from the day the Corporation asks; the Act sets no period ("in such manner and form as the Corporation may
-- determine"), so the days the Corporation allows are an INPUT.
GIVEN `self-insured` IS A BOOLEAN, `the days the Corporation allows` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `RTW party` `RTW act`
DECIDE `s 30(6) -- the employer must furnish the information the Corporation reasonably requires` `self-insured` `the days the Corporation allows` IS
    IF `self-insured`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the employer`
         MUST  `furnish the information the Corporation reasonably requires`
         WITHIN `the days the Corporation allows`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "s 30(6): an employer that is not self-insured must furnish the information the Corporation reasonably requires to assess or determine the claim; maximum penalty $1 500"

-- ss 31(4), 32(2), from the day the Corporation receives an income support claim. s 31(4) is an endeavour, not a duty,
-- so missing the 10 business days is no breach (DO); s 32(2) then makes the Corporation offer interim payments (no period).
GIVEN `the calendar days to the 10th business day after receipt` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `RTW party` `RTW act`
DECIDE `ss 31(4), 32(2) -- if the claim is not decided within 10 business days, interim payments must be offered` `the calendar days to the 10th business day after receipt` IS
    PARTY `the Corporation`
    DO    `determine the claim`
    WITHIN `the calendar days to the 10th business day after receipt`
    LEST
        PARTY `the Corporation`
        MUST  `offer to make interim payments`

-- s 18(1), (2): no period is set; the duty lasts while it applies.
GIVEN `the duty applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `RTW party` `RTW act`
DECIDE `s 18(1), (2) -- the pre-injury employer must provide suitable employment` `the duty applies` IS
    IF `the duty applies`
    THEN PARTY `the employer`
         MUST  `provide suitable employment`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 18(4b)-(4e), from the day the employer receives the subsection (3) notice. The day counts for "1 month" are given by
-- the caller for the case (they depend on the dates). After a written reply, the worker's month runs from the reply; with
-- no reply, from the end of the employer's month (s 18(4d)(b)). Missing the employer's month is a failure of s 18(4b), whose
-- consequence the Act gives as the worker's right to go to the Tribunal, not a penalty.
DECLARE `Subsection (3) rule facts` HAS
    `the worker may apply to the Tribunal`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the calendar days in the month after receipt`                   IS A NUMBER
    `the calendar days in the month after the reply`                 IS A NUMBER
    `the calendar days in the month after the employer's month ends` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the days` IS A NUMBER, f IS A `Subsection (3) rule facts`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `RTW party` `RTW act`
`s 18(4d) -- the worker may apply to the Tribunal within` `the days` `for` f MEANS
    IF f's `the worker may apply to the Tribunal`
    THEN PARTY `the worker`
         MAY   `apply to the Tribunal for an order to provide employment`
         WITHIN `the days`
    ELSE FULFILLED

GIVEN r IS A `Written reply`, f IS A `Subsection (3) rule facts`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `RTW party` `RTW act`
`s 18(4c), (4d)(a) -- after the employer's written reply` r `for` f MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `it refuses, with its grounds` THEN `s 18(4d) -- the worker may apply to the Tribunal within` (f's `the calendar days in the month after the reply`) `for` f
    OTHERWISE
            (PARTY `the employer` MUST `provide suitable employment`)
        RAND
            (`s 18(4d) -- the worker may apply to the Tribunal within` (f's `the calendar days in the month after the reply`) `for` f)

GIVEN f IS A `Subsection (3) rule facts`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `RTW party` `RTW act`
DECIDE `s 18(4b), (4d) -- the employer must reply in writing within 1 month, and the worker may then go to the Tribunal` f IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `notify the worker in writing` r
    WITHIN f's `the calendar days in the month after receipt`
    HENCE `s 18(4c), (4d)(a) -- after the employer's written reply` r `for` f
    LEST  `s 18(4d) -- the worker may apply to the Tribunal within` (f's `the calendar days in the month after the employer's month ends`) `for` f

-- s 20, from the day notice of the proposed termination is given: the employer must not terminate within the 28 days.
GIVEN `notice is required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `RTW party` `RTW act`
DECIDE `s 20 -- after notice, no termination for 28 days` `notice is required` IS
    IF `notice is required`
    THEN PARTY `the employer`
         SHANT `terminate the worker's employment`
         WITHIN 27
         LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "s 20(1): the employer must give the worker and the Corporation at least 28 days notice of the proposed termination"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 20, before any notice: the employer must not terminate at all.
GIVEN `notice is required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `RTW party` `RTW act`
DECIDE `s 20 -- without notice, no termination` `notice is required` IS
    IF `notice is required`
    THEN PARTY `the employer`
         SHANT `terminate the worker's employment`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "s 20(1): the employer must not terminate an injured worker's employment without first giving the worker and the Corporation at least 28 days notice"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 43(1): no period; a failure is a ground for discontinuing payments (s 48(2)(f), (3)(e)(ii)), not a breach as such.
GIVEN `the capacity` IS A `Work capacity`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `RTW party` `RTW act`
DECIDE `s 43(1) -- a worker with current work capacity must make reasonable efforts to return to work` `the capacity` IS
    CONSIDER `the capacity`
    WHEN `a current work capacity` THEN
        PARTY `the worker`
        MUST  `make reasonable efforts to return to work`
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED

-- s 48(9), (10), from the day the worker receives notice of a decision to reduce or discontinue. Applying is the worker's
-- choice (DO, with no breach if not used); if the worker applies and elects within 1 month, the payments must continue or
-- be reinstated "until the matter first comes before a member of the Tribunal" (no period). Not past 104 weeks from the
-- first incapacity, except for a seriously injured worker (s 48(10)).
GIVEN `the days in the month after the notice` IS A NUMBER, `past 104 weeks and not a seriously injured worker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `RTW party` `RTW act`
DECIDE `s 48(9) -- an application and election within 1 month keeps weekly payments going` `the days in the month after the notice` `past 104 weeks and not a seriously injured worker` IS
    PARTY `the worker`
    DO    `apply to the Tribunal for review and elect that weekly payments continue`
    WITHIN `the days in the month after the notice`
    HENCE `s 48(9)(a) -- the payments continue` `past 104 weeks and not a seriously injured worker`
    LEST  FULFILLED

GIVEN `past 104 weeks and not a seriously injured worker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `RTW party` `RTW act`
`s 48(9)(a) -- the payments continue` `past 104 weeks and not a seriously injured worker` MEANS
    IF `past 104 weeks and not a seriously injured worker`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the Corporation`
         MUST  `continue or reinstate the weekly payments`
